From: Project Luma <project-luma@local>
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: milos: correct FP6 front camera rotation

Physical preview and a native-resolution RAW capture show the Fairphone 6
front camera is inverted when described as 270 degrees.  Correct the sensor
mounting metadata by rotating it 180 degrees to 90.  Preview mirroring remains
an application policy and is deliberately not encoded as sensor geometry.

--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/milos-fairphone-fp6.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/milos-fairphone-fp6.dts
@@ -733,7 +733,7 @@
 		pinctrl-0 = <&cam_mclk3_default &s5kkd1sp_reset_default>;
 
 		orientation = <0>;
-		rotation = <270>;
+		rotation = <90>;
 
 		port {
 			s5kkd1sp_ep: endpoint {
-- 
2.51.0
